  "chunks": [
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Renewable Energy Engineering (هندسة الطاقة المتجددة) — B.Sc. study plan 2025/2026, Faculty of Engineering & Design, Middle East University.\nThe degree requires 162 credit hours in total:\n- University requirements: 18 credit hours (compulsory)\n- University electives: 6 credit hours\n- Faculty requirements: 24 credit hours (group A: 6, group B: 18 — mathematics, physics, chemistry)\n- Area of study (major) requirements: 91 credit hours\n- Ancillary (supporting) courses: 14 credit hours\n- Area of study (major) electives: 9 credit hours\nRemedial courses (Arabic, English, computer skills) are taken only when required and are not counted in the 162 hours.\nThe plan includes external Field Training (after 115 completed credit hours) followed by a two-part graduation project (Graduation Project I requires Field Training, then Graduation Project II)."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Renewable Energy Engineering study plan 2025/2026 — approvals and signatories.\nFaculty Council decision 04/06-2025/2026, adopted 06/11/2025. Deans' Council decision 08/15-2025/2026, adopted 30/12/2025.\nHead of Department: Dr. Samer Mohammad As'ad. Dean of the Faculty: Prof. Ayman Abdel Salam Awad. Director of Admissions and Registration: Mrs. Nadia Al-Bakri."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Renewable Energy Engineering — energy technology courses in the 2025/2026 study plan:\nIntroduction to Renewable Energy (1912601), Introduction to Solar Energy (1912602), Solar Thermal Energy (1913601), Photovoltaic Energy (الطاقة الكهروضوئية, 1914601) with Solar Energy Lab (1914602), Wind Energy (طاقة الرياح, 1914603) with Wind Energy Lab (1914604), Energy Conversion and Storage (1914703), Power Systems (1913702), Power Electronics with lab (1914701/1914702), Energy Efficiency and Economics (1915801), Energy Management and Regulations (1915802), Environmental Impact of Energy (1915803), Design and Simulation I and II (1914303/1914304). Electives include Hydroelectric Energy, Green Buildings, Water Desalination by Solar Energy, Advanced Photovoltaic Systems, Smart Grid Systems and Artificial Intelligence in Renewable Energy."
    }
  ],
